{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nOnce coordinator results are authoritative, preview/log/manifest consumers need a stable additive contract and state must advance only for proven postconditions. Deferred or ambiguous work cannot be reported as applied.\n\n## Outcome\nFinalize versioned lifecycle/retry/fuse outcome sections, exact pass tallies/cursor behavior, and redacted bounded diagnostics while preserving existing mutation fields.\n\n## Plan\n1. Render versioned lifecycle intents, logical/physical attempts, delay source/value, budget, failure scope, disposition, `retry_not_before`, fuse state, and exact ticket/pass outcomes.\n2. Preserve the existing mutation fields/array/hash and make additive sections ignorable by older readers.\n3. Advance cursor, baseline, binding, and last-pass state only after proven postconditions. Deferred, failed, skipped, and `commit_unknown` work stays eligible for later re-observation.\n4. Pin applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered tallies and exit semantics for mixed passes and delivery failure.\n5. Redact secrets and bound every diagnostic field and collection.\n\n## Testing\nGolden preview/log/manifest fixtures cover every disposition and mixed pass. State spies assert exact writes and next-pass eligibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Existing mutation fields, array bytes, and canonical hash remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Additive versioned output includes every named lifecycle/retry/fuse/outcome field.\n- [ ] Cursor, baseline, and binding state advance only for proven postconditions.\n- [ ] Deferred, failed, skipped, and `commit_unknown` work is not counted as applied and remains eligible next pass.\n- [ ] Mixed-pass tallies and exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Logs and manifests contain no secret or unbounded diagnostic content.\n\n## Out of scope\nRoute removal and portable end-to-end/documentation completion.\n\n## Inherited invariant — pre-observation repair boundary (folded in from insectile-modest-martin, 2026-08-19)\n\nOperator decision: `insectile-modest-martin` (d7b9-ac42) is CLOSED and its requirement now lives\nhere. This ticket edits `reconcile.py`, which sits at **799 of the 800-line cap**, so it must\nperform a behaviour-preserving extraction (extract along an existing call-graph seam; NEVER raise\nthe limit). That extraction must preserve one specific ordering invariant that is easy to break\nsilently.\n\n**The invariant.** The call\n`binding_store.repair_at_write_boundary(persist=persist, scoped=bool(scoped_ids))` must remain:\n\n- **AFTER** the under-lock staleness validation (`ensure_selection_current`) — a pass whose\n  selection is stale has not established that its view is current and has no standing to repair; and\n- **BEFORE** the pass's first remote issue fetch (`fetcher.fetch_snapshot` / `compute_snapshot`).\n\nThe pre-observation half is the one with teeth. A durable tombstone is authoritative retirement\nintent. A pass that fetched first could observe the retired issue answer 200 and then complete that\nissue's retirement in the same breath as fresh evidence that it is alive; repairing first keeps the\nrecorded decision from racing a later observation. **Move the call after the fetch and the repair\nstill runs, still writes correct-looking bytes, and is silently wrong.**\n\n`run_differs.py` is specifically NOT an alternative home: `reconcile._load_snapshots` performs the\nfirst remote fetch inside itself, and both `bind_operation_runtime` and `run_differs()` run after it\nreturns, so no position inside `run_differs.py` can precede remote observation. Recorded in ADR 0099.\n\n**The two tests that are the only guard** (both drive or name `_load_snapshots` directly, so an\nextraction that renames or re-splits that phase WILL force someone to touch them) — in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py`:\n\n- `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` — the behavioural oracle; drives the real\n  load phase with an event recorder and asserts the repair event precedes the fetch event.\n- `test_the_repair_is_invoked_from_reconcile_and_not_from_run_differs` — a structural anchor.\n\nThe tempting shortcut under time pressure is to relax the assertion rather than re-anchor it.\n**Relaxing it is the thing to avoid.**\n\n### Additional acceptance criteria (inherited)\n- [ ] After this change to `reconcile.py`, the repair call still runs after the under-lock staleness\n      gate and before the pass's first remote issue fetch.\n- [ ] `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` still fails when the call is moved to a\n      post-fetch position — demonstrated by SEEDING that move and observing RED, not merely by the\n      suite being green.\n- [ ] If the load phase is renamed or re-split, the boundary tests are RE-ANCHORED to the new\n      structure rather than relaxed, and the ordering assertion survives in a form that still\n      discriminates.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` remains within the 800-line cap without raising the limit.\n- [ ] ADR 0099's invocation-boundary section is updated if the realized position changes shape.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787173972075621001,"uuid":"e9ec57ff-497b-4151-88b5-dfa7ae684716"}